        It mocks <code>/api/property/schedules</code> and shoots 8 states at desktop
        (1440&times;900) and tablet (1194&times;834 with <code>hasTouch</code> — without that flag
        you get the desktop path and aren't testing tablet at all). Extend its fixtures as the
        phases land: a split part-paid and a <span class="mono">pending_dispatch</span> invoice
        for Phase 1, the popover and its cancel confirmation for Phase 3, a
        <code>?mode=reminder</code> run for Phase 4, a re-shot bill for 5–6, a new automation
        shot for 7, an expanded reference row for 8.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:0.7rem">
        It currently collects page errors but <strong>exits zero</strong>. Make it fail hard
        while you're in there.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>After any change to the left column or the rail</h3>
      <p>
        <code>probe-cascade.mjs</code> must stay at 13/13 screens with nothing stuck at
        opacity&nbsp;0, and <code>probe-transitions.mjs</code> at zero chrome remounts and zero
