<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Questions for Oliver</h2>
    <p>Answer before Phase 5. Phases 1–4 can start now.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="q">
    <div class="q-n">01</div>
    <div class="q-b">
      <span class="q-t">Split was deliberately deferred. Un-defer it?</span>
      <p>The bill's split toggle was logged as a deliberate omission. This plan un-defers it and also adds split to the rent request, which the phone has and desktop never did.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="q">
    <div class="q-n">02</div>
    <div class="q-b">
      <span class="q-t">Should the bill keep its pre-selected charge type?</span>
      <p>Desktop pre-selects "water / utilities", so a bill can go out without the type ever being chosen; the phone forces an explicit pick.</p>
      <p class="rec">Recommend keeping it — all five chips are visible at once and the design shows a selected chip — but this is the one I'd happily reverse.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="q">
    <div class="q-n">03</div>
    <div class="q-b">
      <span class="q-t">Scope chip: wire it or delete it?</span>
      <p class="rec">Recommend wiring. A dead control is worse than either outcome.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="q">
    <div class="q-n">04</div>
    <div class="q-b">
      <span class="q-t">The phone's unreachable screen: wire it up or delete it?</span>
      <p>See below — it's a phone commit either way, not tablet work.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Out of scope: the phone's dead screen</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="panel">
    <p>
      <code>BatchAndAutoScreen</code> implements batch send, schedule management and reminder
      settings on the phone in ~140 lines, and <strong>nothing navigates to it.</strong> The
      subbar covers only tenants / send / bill / external, and there is no
      <code>go('batch')</code> anywhere in <code>client/src</code> — the only surviving reference
      is a <code>busy.batch</code> key in a test fixture. <code>batchMutation</code> is dead with it.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:0.9rem">
      So schedule management and reminder settings are missing from <strong>both</strong> clients,
      and Phase 7 is new functionality rather than parity. Wire it up — a fifth subbar slot,
      which also gives the phone batch send — or delete it, since once Phase 7 lands an
      unreachable duplicate of the same UI is a liability. Either way it's a phone commit and
      doesn't belong in this branch's screen-at-a-time queue.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

